{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_017PAq5ZgZGpiBqbiBmbvEMg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both functions are fixed. Here is my analysis and the fix.\n\n## Root cause\n\nDuckLake's INSERT writes table data through DuckDB's `PhysicalCopyToFile` operator, targeting a **directory** (e.g. `<data_path>/main/events`) with file rotation enabled:\n\n- In `ducklake_insert.cpp`, the unpartitioned write path sets `result.file_path = copy_input.data_path` (the table's data directory), `result.rotate = true`, `result.file_size_bytes = target_file_size`, and `result.overwrite_mode = CopyOverwriteMode::COPY_OVERWRITE_OR_IGNORE`.\n- Because `Rotate()` is true (`file_size_bytes.IsValid()`), `PhysicalCopyToFile::GetGlobalSinkState` enters the `partition_output || per_thread_output || Rotate()` branch. There it does:\n  ```cpp\n  if (fs.FileExists(file_path)) {            // file_path == \".../main/events\"\n      if (overwrite_mode == COPY_OVERWRITE)  // ours is OVERWRITE_OR_IGNORE, not COPY_OVERWRITE\n          fs.RemoveFile(file_path);\n      else\n          throw IOException(\"Cannot write to \\\"%s\\\" - it exists and is a file, not a directory! ...\");\n  }\n  ```\n\nSo everything hinges on what `FileExists` returns for a **directory**:\n\n- First INSERT: `main/events` doesn't exist yet → `FileExists` false, `DirectoryExists` false → `CreateDirectory` → parquet written. ✅\n- Second INSERT: `main/events` now exists as a directory. `FileExists` should return **false** (it's a directory, not a file) so the code proceeds to `DirectoryExists`/`CheckDirectory`. Instead it returns **true**, and since the mode is `OVERWRITE_OR_IGNORE` (not `COPY_OVERWRITE`), it throws. ❌\n\nTracing `FileExists` down the WASM stack:\n- `WebFileSystem::FileExists` → `duckdb_web_fs_file_exists` (an `extern \"C\"` runtime hook under `EMSCRIPTEN`) → `NATIVE_FS->FileExists`, implemented in JS by the node runtime's `checkFile`.\n- The node runtime's `checkFile` was `return fs.existsSync(path)`. **`fs.existsSync` returns `true` for directories as well as files**, so once the table directory exists, `FileExists` wrongly reports it as a file.\n\nThis diverges from native DuckDB semantics: `LocalFileSystem::FileExists` returns true only when `S_ISREG(status.st_mode)` (a regular file), and `DirectoryExists` only when `S_ISDIR`. `checkDirectory` had the mirror-image bug (it would report a regular file as an existing directory).\n\n## The fix\n\nIn `runtime_node.ts`, `checkFile` now returns true only for a regular file, and `checkDirectory` only for a directory — matching `LocalFileSystem`'s `S_ISREG`/`S_ISDIR` behavior:\n\n```ts\n// checkFile\nif (!fs.existsSync(path)) return false;\nreturn fs.statSync(path).isFile();\n\n// checkDirectory\nif (!fs.existsSync(path)) return false;\nreturn fs.statSync(path).isDirectory();\n```\n\nI used an `existsSync` guard + `statSync` rather than `statSync(path, { throwIfNoEntry: false })` because (a) the workspace pins multiple `@types/node` versions (including `^12`) where that overload isn't typed under `strict` mode, and (b) the surrounding `catch` would otherwise call `failWith` on a normal `ENOENT` for a legitimately-absent path.\n\nI did **not** touch the browser runtime: it uses a buffer-based filesystem where `checkDirectory` is hardcoded `false` and `createDirectory` is a no-op, so it has no real directory tree and isn't subject to this bug. The reported failure is the node runtime.\n\n## Sources\n- duckdb · src/execution/operator/persistent/physical_copy_to_file.cpp · lines 1680–1702 (`GetGlobalSinkState`, the `FileExists` check + IOException)\n- duckdb · src/common/local_file_system.cpp · lines 70–80 (`LocalFileSystem::FileExists`, `S_ISREG`)\n- duckdb · src/common/local_file_system.cpp · lines 167–178 (Windows `FileExists`, `S_IFREG`)\n- duckdb · src/common/local_file_system.cpp · lines 698–711 (`LocalFileSystem::DirectoryExists`, `S_ISDIR`)\n- ducklake · src/storage/ducklake_insert.cpp · lines 557–577 (`file_path`/`rotate`/`overwrite_mode` setup for the data directory)\n- ducklake · src/storage/ducklake_insert.cpp · lines 671–695 (mapping `DuckLakeCopyOptions` onto `PhysicalCopyToFile`)\n- duckdb-wasm · lib/src/io/web_filesystem.cc · lines 1002–1006 (`WebFileSystem::FileExists` → `duckdb_web_fs_file_exists`)\n- duckdb-wasm · lib/src/io/web_filesystem.cc · lines 104–162 (`RT_FN` macro: `extern \"C\"` under EMSCRIPTEN; `NATIVE_FS` only for native tests)\n- duckdb-wasm · lib/src/io/web_filesystem.cc · lines 62–93 (`NATIVE_FS = FileSystem::CreateLocal()` guarded by `#ifndef EMSCRIPTEN`)\n- duckdb-wasm · packages/duckdb-wasm/src/bindings/runtime_node.ts · `checkFile`/`checkDirectory` (lines 233–247, 301–317 — the buggy `fs.existsSync` and the fix)\n- duckdb-wasm · packages/duckdb-wasm/src/bindings/runtime_browser.ts · lines 502–518, 738–746 (`checkFile` HTTP/S3 path; `checkDirectory` hardcoded false, `createDirectory` no-op — why browser runtime is unaffected)\n- duckdb-wasm · packages/duckdb-wasm-app/package.json · line 45 (`@types/node` `^22`); yarn.lock `@types/node` entries incl. `^12` (rationale for avoiding `throwIfNoEntry`)"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":526,"cache_read_input_tokens":52021,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":526},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3c4350dd-ce4a-4df6-94b3-4f1719fce8fc","uuid":"13557c0a-9ad6-494c-92a6-6d1e1553002c","request_id":"req_011CbqygaSh5ksH8JB8QYfzH"}
